<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="open-pilgrimages" version="1.1"><metadata><name>Camino Portugués da Costa (Coastal — Portuguese section)</name><desc>The Portuguese coastal section of the Camino Portugués da Costa, running from Porto along the Atlantic coast through Vila do Conde, Esposende, Viana do Castelo, and Caminha to the border ferry crossing at A Guarda. Approximately 110 km in 5 stages. The Spanish continuation through Oia, Baiona, Vigo, and Redondela (where it merges with the Central route to Santiago) is currently a stub — full Spanish-side data is planned for a future release. The Coastal Way is the second-most-walked Camino Portugués route after the Central, accounting for ~17% of all 2025 Compostelas — nearly tied with Central. Grew from very small numbers in the 2010s to 89,511 pilgrims in 2025.</desc><copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"><license>https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/</license></copyright><link href="https://open.pilgrimag.es/camino-portugues"><text>Camino Portugués da Costa (Coastal — Portuguese section)</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Camino Portugués da Costa (Coastal — Portuguese section)</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="41.140829" lon="-8.610069"/><trkpt lat="41.140742" lon="-8.609852"/><trkpt lat="41.140719" lon="-8.609747"/><trkpt lat="41.140798" lon="-8.610183"/><trkpt lat="41.140800" lon="-8.610164"/><trkpt lat="41.140809" lon="-8.610119"/><trkpt lat="41.140810" lon="-8.610112"/><trkpt lat="41.140810" lon="-8.610110"/><trkpt lat="41.140814" lon="-8.610094"/><trkpt lat="41.140821" lon="-8.610076"/><trkpt lat="41.140829" lon="-8.610069"/><trkpt lat="41.140612" lon="-8.611374"/><trkpt lat="41.140620" lon="-8.611321"/><trkpt lat="41.140636" lon="-8.611200"/><trkpt lat="41.140662" lon="-8.611041"/><trkpt lat="41.140668" lon="-8.610997"/><trkpt lat="41.140746" lon="-8.610490"/><trkpt lat="41.140757" lon="-8.610433"/><trkpt lat="41.140779" lon="-8.610303"/><trkpt lat="41.140781" lon="-8.610288"/>